# ArtNet Lightshow is configured in the app, not the environment.
#
# Everything — outputs, MIDI, Spotify and Deezer, playback sources, the
# analysis, the bind address, port and access token — is set in its Rig,
# Sources and Settings views (http://localhost:3000/#settings) and stored in
# config/settings.json (mode 0600, gitignored). Anything not set uses the
# built-in default, so there is nothing to copy or fill in here to get started.
#
# If you have an old .env, the server names the variables it is ignoring at
# startup. Set those values once in the app, then delete them.
#
# A .env in the directory the server is started from is still read (by Node's
# own loader; a variable already set in the environment wins). What it can
# usefully hold:
#
#DEBUG_MIDI=1                    # log every incoming MIDI message
#ARTNET_PYTHON=/path/to/python   # the Python that runs the analysis, over the one found
#LIGHTSHOW_CONFIG_DIR=/srv/show  # where settings, the show, cues and the MIDI map live
#LIGHTSHOW_CACHE_DIR=/srv/cache  # where the analysis cache lives
